---
// src/components/sections/SpotifySection.astro
---
<div id="spotify" class="os-content">
  
  <!-- INTRO SPOTIFY -->
  <section class="video-section" id="intro-spotify">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="section-kicker">// personalización avanzada</p>
      <h2>Cómo instalar Spicetify</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">Spicetify is a multiplatform command-line tool to customize the official Spotify client.[cite: 1]</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AVISO SPOTIFY -->
  <section class="warning-strip">
    <div class="warning-inner">
      <span class="warning-icon">ℹ️</span>
      <p><strong>Before First Run:</strong> If this is a fresh Spotify install, open Spotify and log in for at least 60 seconds before running Spicetify.[cite: 1] This allows Spotify to generate the files that Spicetify needs to function.[cite: 1]</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PASOS SPOTIFY -->
  <section class="steps-section" id="pasos-spotify">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="section-kicker">// guía de instalación windows</p>
      <h2>Los pasos para instalar y usar Spicetify</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      
      <article class="step" data-step="1">
        <button class="step-head" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="step-num">01</span><span class="step-title">Instalar Spicetify CLI</span><span class="step-time">PowerShell</span><span class="step-chevron">▾</span>
        </button>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-effect"><strong>¿Qué sucede al hacer esto?</strong> Se descarga e instala la herramienta principal de Spicetify en tu sistema mediante PowerShell (Recomendado).[cite: 1]</div>
          <ol class="action-list">
            <li>Abrí una ventana de PowerShell.</li>
            <li>Copiá y pegá el siguiente comando:</li>
            <code>iwr -useb https://raw.githubusercontent.com/spicetify/cli/main/install.ps1 | iex</code>[cite: 1]
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="step" data-step="2">
        <button class="step-head" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="step-num">02</span><span class="step-title">Instalar el Marketplace</span><span class="step-time">PowerShell</span><span class="step-chevron">▾</span>
        </button>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-effect"><strong>¿Qué sucede al hacer esto?</strong> The Spicetify Marketplace gives you a tab in Spotify’s sidebar to browse and install themes, extensions, and snippets.[cite: 1]</div>
          <ol class="action-list">
            <li>En la misma ventana de PowerShell, ejecutá:</li>
            <code>iwr -useb https://raw.githubusercontent.com/spicetify/marketplace/main/resources/install.ps1 | iex</code>[cite: 1]
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="step" data-step="3">
        <button class="step-head" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="step-num">03</span><span class="step-title">Aplicar temas y extensiones</span><span class="step-time">Uso Básico</span><span class="step-chevron">▾</span>
        </button>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-effect"><strong>¿Qué sucede al hacer esto?</strong> Comienzas a personalizar tu cliente de Spotify.</div>
          <ol class="action-list">
            <li>After installing Spicetify and Marketplace, you can customize Spotify using themes and extensions from the Marketplace tab in Spotify’s sidebar.[cite: 1]</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="step" data-step="4">
        <button class="step-head" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="step-num">04</span><span class="step-title">Actualizaciones futuras</span><span class="step-time">Mantenimiento</span><span class="step-chevron">▾</span>
        </button>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-effect"><strong>¿Qué sucede al hacer esto?</strong> Spotify updates periodically. After a Spotify update, you’ll need to re-apply Spicetify.[cite: 1]</div>
          <ol class="action-list">
            <li>Abrí PowerShell y ejecutá: <code>spicetify backup apply</code>[cite: 1]</li>
            <li>If that doesn’t work, Spicetify itself may need an update: <code>spicetify update</code>[cite: 1]</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>
</div>